# Sprint Closeout Protocol — AI-Investor

description: This rule defines the mandatory process to execute when a sprint is marked as COMPLETE.
A sprint is NOT considered fully closed until this protocol has been executed and validated.

alwaysApply: false
---

# Trigger Condition

This protocol must be applied when the user states:

- "Sprint X is complete"
- "Close Sprint X"
- "Finish Sprint X"
- "Sprint X done"

---

# Blocking conditions (do NOT closeout)

**Stop and report gaps** if any of the following are true:

- Sprint-specific Definition of Done is not fully satisfied (`.cursor/rules/60-definition-of-done.mdc`)
- Current sprint exit criteria in `docs/roadmap/AI-INVESTOR-ROADMAP.md` have open checkboxes
- `docs/quality/SPRINT-X-CLOSEOUT.md` still shows epics or stories in progress
- Only design documentation landed without required implementation and tests (Epic 3/4 rule for Sprint 1)
- Tests or build are failing

**Sprint 1 reopen precedent:** Closeout was run prematurely on 2026-06-24 after Epic 2 only. Do not repeat — verify Epics 3–5 before closing a sprint.

**Sprint 1 status:** ✅ Complete (2026-06-24). Full record: [`docs/quality/SPRINT-1-CLOSEOUT.md`](docs/quality/SPRINT-1-CLOSEOUT.md). Apply this protocol to **Sprint 2+** closeouts.

---

# Step 1 — Sprint Review (What was built)

Summarize:

- What features were implemented
- What architecture changes were introduced
- What refactoring occurred
- What tests were added or improved
- What remains deferred to a future sprint (with roadmap IDs)

Output must be structured as:

```markdown
## Sprint X Review

### Delivered
- ...

### Architecture changes
- ...

### Tests added/improved
- ...

### Deferred
- ...
```

---

# Step 2 — Architecture Consistency Check

Evaluate:

- Does implementation match `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md`?
- Are service / provider / repository boundaries respected?
- Is UI separated from business logic (no direct `fetch` in components)?
- Are there any architectural violations?

If violations exist:

- List them explicitly
- Suggest remediation steps

Output:

```markdown
## Architecture consistency

| Check | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Layer boundaries | Pass / Fail | ... |
| Repository separation | Pass / Fail | ... |
| ... | ... | ... |
```

---

# Step 3 — Documentation Audit

Check and update per `.cursor/rules/30-documentation.mdc`:

## Required updates

| Document | Action |
|---|---|
| `docs/roadmap/AI-INVESTOR-ROADMAP.md` | Mark sprint complete; append sprint history |
| `docs/quality/SPRINT-X-CLOSEOUT.md` | Mark ✅ Complete; final epic table |
| `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` | Update if structure or flows changed |
| `docs/architecture/AI-INVESTOR-CONTEXT.md` | Update if scope or epic status changed |
| `README.md` | Update if user-facing behavior or doc index changed |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Update active sprint line |

## Conditional updates (when applicable)

| Document | When |
|---|---|
| `docs/adr/*.md` | Architectural decisions made (auth, API, persistence, CI, etc.) |
| `docs/architecture/repository-pattern.md` | Persistence layer changed |
| `docs/security/authentication.md`, `docs/security/rbac.md` | Epic 3 implemented |
| `docs/api/validation.md`, `docs/api/error-model.md` | Epic 4 implemented |
| `docs/quality/TESTING-STANDARDS.md` | Test strategy or commands changed |
| `docs/devops/CI-CD.md` | Pipeline or quality gates changed |
| `docs/ai/*` | AI workflows or agents changed |
| `docs/quality/CODEREVIEW.md` | Sprint review changes quality assessment or technical debt |
| `docs/database/prisma.md` | Seed data or schema changed (e.g. admin watchlist) |

## Post-closeout remediations

If a code review (`CODEREVIEW.md`) lands **after** initial closeout:

1. Fix blocking/high findings before merge
2. Update `SPRINT-X-CLOSEOUT.md` with a post-closeout section
3. Sync `60-definition-of-done.mdc` epic criteria if new acceptance rules emerge
4. Re-run lint, test, build; update CODEREVIEW verdict

Sprint 1 example: CODEREVIEW remediations (2026-06-24) — login credential hygiene, admin watchlist seed, session-aware `WatchlistContext`.

Output:

```markdown
## Documentation audit

| Document | Updated | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| ... | Yes / No / N/A | ... |
```

---

# Step 4 — ADR Generation Check

Identify if any of the following occurred:

- New service layer or repository boundary
- New database schema or model
- Authentication or RBAC changes
- API validation or error-model changes
- Testing strategy changes
- AI agent design changes
- CI/CD pipeline changes

If YES:

- Propose ADR titles
- Provide short summaries for each ADR
- Create or update ADRs as part of closeout — do not defer if the decision already shipped

**Sprint 1 expected ADRs:** auth strategy (P2-04) → **ADR-010** ✅; API error/validation (P3-01) → **ADR-011** ✅

Output:

```markdown
## ADR check

| Decision | ADR | Action |
|---|---|---|
| ... | ADR-NNN | Create / Update / N/A |
```

---

# Step 5 — Test Coverage Review

Evaluate:

- Are new features covered by tests?
- Are API endpoints tested (happy path + key failures)?
- Are auth/RBAC paths tested (401 / 403) if Epic 3 shipped?
- Are validation `details` and error `code` asserted if Epic 4 shipped?
- Are critical flows covered in Playwright?
- Are there missing edge cases?

Output:

```markdown
## Test coverage

| Area | Status | Gaps |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | ... | ... |
| API routes | ... | ... |
| Integration | ... | ... |
| E2E | ... | ... |
```

---

# Step 6 — Quality Assessment (Staff-Level Evaluation)

Evaluate the sprint against Staff/Principal SDET expectations:

- Is architecture scalable?
- Is code maintainable?
- Are abstractions justified?
- Is complexity controlled?
- Are responsibilities well-separated?

Output:

```markdown
## Quality assessment

**Strengths:** ...
**Risks:** ...
**Interview narrative (60s):** ...
```

---

# Step 7 — Technical Debt Identification

List:

- Duplicated logic
- Over-engineered abstractions
- Missing error handling
- Tight coupling issues
- Temporary shortcuts taken during sprint

Cross-reference `docs/quality/CODEREVIEW.md` if a review exists for the sprint.

Output:

```markdown
## Technical debt

| ID | Severity | Item | Target |
|---|---|---|---|
| ... | ... | ... | ... |
```

---

# Step 8 — AI Usage Review

Evaluate AI-assisted development:

- Where AI was used effectively
- Where AI introduced risk or inefficiency
- Where prompts should be improved
- Where automation could be added

Output:

```markdown
## AI usage review

- Effective: ...
- Risks: ...
- Prompt/doc improvements: ...
```

---

# Step 9 — Next Sprint Preparation

Generate:

## Recommended next sprint focus

Based on `docs/roadmap/AI-INVESTOR-ROADMAP.md` + current state.

## Suggested backlog items

- Features
- Refactoring
- Tests
- Documentation
- Infrastructure improvements

Output:

```markdown
## Next sprint prep

**Recommended focus:** Sprint N — ...
**Top backlog items:** ...
```

---

# Step 10 — Sprint Closure Validation

Before marking sprint as complete, verify:

- [ ] Code is merged or committed to the integration branch
- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
- [ ] `npm run build` passes
- [ ] `npm test` passes (and integration/E2E if applicable to sprint scope)
- [ ] Sprint-specific Definition of Done satisfied (`.cursor/rules/60-definition-of-done.mdc`)
- [ ] All exit criteria in `docs/roadmap/AI-INVESTOR-ROADMAP.md` for this sprint are checked
- [ ] `docs/quality/SPRINT-X-CLOSEOUT.md` updated to ✅ Complete
- [ ] Required docs updated (Step 3)
- [ ] ADRs created or explicitly N/A (Step 4)
- [ ] Behavior changes verified against running app where applicable
- [ ] No critical TODOs left unresolved in shipped epics
- [ ] Architecture consistency check passed (Step 2)
- [ ] Sprint review completed (Step 1)
- [ ] Code review completed if sprint shipped auth/security/API surface (`docs/quality/CODEREVIEW.md`)

**Sprint 1 additional checks (reference — all satisfied 2026-06-24):**

- [x] Epic 3 — Auth.js + RBAC implemented (not design-only)
- [x] Epic 4 — Zod validation + central error handler on all routes
- [x] Epic 5 — Auth/API test coverage + doc sync complete
- [x] CODEREVIEW remediations — login UI credential hygiene, admin watchlist seed, session-aware client
- [x] `npm run lint`, `npm test` (99), `npm run build` at closeout

**Sprint 1 — open follow-ups (not blocking closeout):**

- [ ] Merge `feature/API-Foundation` → `main`
- [ ] Re-run `db:seed` locally after admin watchlist migration (if DB predates fix)
- [ ] TD-02 user-visible watchlist errors → Sprint 2

If any checkbox is missing:

- Sprint is **NOT** complete
- List blocking items explicitly
- Do **NOT** mark sprint history as complete in `docs/roadmap/AI-INVESTOR-ROADMAP.md`

