# Core Principle

This protocol ensures:

- No sprint ends without reflection
- No architecture drift
- No undocumented decisions
- Continuous improvement of engineering quality
- Staff-level discipline in execution

---

# Important Instruction for AI Assistants

When executing this rule:

- Be strict and objective
- Do not assume completion if evidence is missing
- Prefer identifying gaps over false completeness
- Treat this as a real engineering sprint review in a production team
- If the user asks to close a sprint but DoD is incomplete, refuse closeout and list blockers — cite `60-definition-of-done.mdc` and `docs/quality/SPRINT-X-CLOSEOUT.md`
